<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  VireoBoo, the mascot of Watube 26.12 "Vireo": a Bangboo of our own, drawn the way that
  world draws them (thick ink outline, flat cel-shaded shadows, a big shell of a head with a
  screen for a face, stubby limbs) but its own character. A vireo is a small songbird, so it
  has a tuft of feathers on its head and a little amber beak under its screen; its happy
  eyes are the Watube green. One mechanical ear is bent at the tip, headphones rest round
  its neck, and the play mark is sewn on its belly. Its right arm is the group "arm" (pivot
  at the shoulder), raised and waved by vireoboo_wave.xml.
-->
